.TH "HTMLCANVASELEMENT.WEBGLCONTEXTCREATIONERROR_EVENT" "3JS" "October 27, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
HTMLCanvasElement.webglcontextcreationerror_event \- HTMLCanvasElement:
webglcontextcreationerror event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]webglcontextcreationerror\f[B]\f[R] event of the WebGL
API is fired if the user agent is unable to create a
\f[CR]WebGLRenderingContext\f[R] context.
.PP
This event has a \f[CR]WebGLContextEvent.statusMessage\f[R] property,
which can contain a platform dependent string with more information
about the failure.
.PP
This event does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqwebglcontextcreationerror\(dq, (event) => { })
.EE
.PP
Alternatively, assign to the event handler property of the interface:
.IP
.EX
onwebglcontextcreationerror = (event) => { }
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A \f[CR]WebGLContextEvent\f[R].
Inherits from \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH EXAMPLE
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] canvas = document.getElementById(\(dqcanvas\(dq);

canvas.addEventListener(\(dqwebglcontextcreationerror\(dq, (e) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(e.statusMessage || \(dqUnknown error\(dq);
});

\f[B]const\f[R] gl = canvas.getContext(\(dqwebgl\(dq);
\f[I]// logs statusMessage or \(dqUnknown error\(dq if unable to create WebGL context\f[R]
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
